WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.844
Editors, welcome to the next era of Premiere,

00:00:02.844 --> 00:00:06.320
your video creation process in one end-to-end platform.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.840
Let's get into it.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.722
First up, Color Mode, a brand new tab

00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:16.060
in Premiere built just for color.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.060
The grade is so important.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:20.522
With Color Mode, you get a pro color workflow,

00:00:20.522 --> 00:00:22.095
you can explore a look, push it,

00:00:22.095 --> 00:00:24.160
then refine and nail it right in Premiere.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.960
Next up, Generative Media Tool.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.344
Now, you can generate video, images, soundscapes,

00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:32.900
and music right on your own timeline.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.527
What I like is that it uses your edit as context

00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:38.920
so you get closer to what you're picturing from the very first prompt.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.740
Some audio problems used to be permanent.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:42.780
Not anymore.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.642
Premiere's new AI audio tools help edit

00:00:45.642 --> 00:00:48.640
and adjust audio with new levels of precision.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.680
Okay, I need this one.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.488
Sometimes I have to re-record voiceover fast on my phone,

00:00:53.488 --> 00:00:56.300
and the sounds of the city are going crazy in the background.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.654
With the new AI audio tools in Premiere, I can clean up rough audio in a click

00:01:00.654 --> 00:01:02.440
and untangle overlapping sounds.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.560
And last, Premiere AI Assistant Beta.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.420
Put it on the work around the work.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.284
Organizing bins and syncing clips

00:01:09.284 --> 00:01:10.580
used to eat my first hour.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.860
Now, I hand that off and get straight to the cut.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.420
So, which of these saves an edit you'd have given up on?

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.720
The audio tools.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.280
That interview with the noisy room I can now use.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.418
And, as always, it is still your judgment

00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:26.680
that decides what makes the cut.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.040
That's the update.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.040
Open and update Premiere to try them out now.
